Root cause:
The bug was caused by improper management of floating objects in the context of the Groonga database extension for Ruby. Specifically, the crash occurred because the floating objects were not being correctly registered and unregistered, leading to potential memory access violations when these objects were accessed after they were supposed to be cleaned up. The patch introduced mechanisms to ensure that floating objects are properly registered and unregistered, preventing the crash that resulted from accessing invalid memory.
